content.text:
Small phone 320x568 issues:
- Wave card is too narrow, text wraps: "ONDA 1 / 4 / cri..." clipped behind XP. Need fix top layout for small screens. Health card and level card crowd; wave card under brand but width limited by flex? The top row has left column (brand+wave) and status (level+health). At 320 width, level card 94 + health 112 + gaps + left wave ~? The wave card gets narrow because status consumes. It's showing "ONDA 1" and "4 cri..." cut.

- XP bar at 112px overlaps wave card (ends ~128) and covers text. Need global top layout redesign for narrow screens:
  - Put XP bar lower, e.g., top 132px at small. Wave card needs width ~100px min; brand left.
  - Better: on <=600px, hide the wave card's "enemies" secondary line or move wave indicator to below brand? Still clipping. Could make top layout stack: Row 1: brand + level + health; Row 2: wave + XP? Hmm.

Let's rethink HUD mobile portrait layout for clarity:
Top:
- Brand top-left.
- Level card top-right? Health bar full width below? Currently top row consists left column with brand+wave and right group level+health. At 320, width too tight.

Option for phones <=400px:
- Hide brand? Keep tiny.
- Top row: level card (compact) + health card (flex).
- Wave card centered below, with XP below that. Could be 3 rows but uses vertical space ~150px. Fine on 568.
But on 390x844 current layout works with wave card 127 wide and status 230 wide = 369 + gaps, borderline. At 320 definitely.

Simpler CSS-only fix:
@media(max-width:380px){
 .brand{display:none}
 .top{...}
 .wave-card{...}
 .xpwrap{top:...}
}
But wave card still constrained.

Better restructure HTML top:
<div class="top">
  <div class="brand">...</div>
  <div class="status">level card, health card</div>
</div>
Then wave card and xp in a separate centered "mission" block below top? Actually can reorganize with absolute positioning:
- .brand fixed top-left
- .status top-right
- .wave-card positioned below brand? Hmm.

Could place wave card at top centerbelow top row, and XP below it. On desktop, wave card is top-left, xp top-center. On mobile, maybe:
Top row: brand (row), level+health.
Second row (center): wave card + XP horizontally? A compact pill "ONDA 1 · 4 criaturas" and XP full width under.

Let's adjust only max-width 600:
- .top position relative; left block: brand + wave as now. But make .wave-card position absolute left:0 top:?? Hmm.

At 320, level 78 + health 112 + gap 9 = ~199, plus left wave 100 + gap 12 = 311 + padding 24 = 335 > 320. Need reduce cards: health width 100, level min 70 (font 22), gaps 6, left 100 → 282 + 24 = 306 fits. So reduce mobile sizes and make wave card text single line (hide enemy count? or use a small dot count). But "ONDA 1" width ~65, and "4 criaturas" ~60; card min 100 fits 2 lines if not clipped. It was clipped because left column gets squeezed.

Use mobile CSS:
.top{gap:8px}
.status{gap:6px}
.level-card{min-width:70px;padding:8px 8px}
.health-card{width:clamp(96px,31vw,150px)}
.levelnum{font-size:24px}
.card{padding:8px 9px}
.wave-card{min-width:96px;padding:7px 9px}
.wave-card strong{font-size:12px}
.wave-card small{font-size:9px}
.brand{font-size:8.5px}
At 320: left col width? Brand width "GUARDIÃO DA ARENA" at 8.5px = ~95; wave 96. status: level 70+health 99+6=175; top row gap 8 → 96+175+8=279 + horizontal padding 24 =303. Fits.
