content.text:
Now marker creation in spawnEnemy. Add near state.enemies.push: const marker=document.createElement('div'); marker.className='off'; marker.textContent='▲'; fxLayer.appendChild(marker); e.marker=marker. fxLayer z-index 2, marker 3 but inside fxLayer stacking context z2 under HUD? HUD no z-index (position fixed, stacking auto) likely overlay? HUD appears above canvas, fxLayer appended body after HUD and z2, so fxLayer above HUD maybe; markers could overlay HUD. We clamp y. Fine. damage numbers z2 inside.

Death removal. Restart loop removal. Also enemies cleared by restart loop; remove markers.

Frame update markers:
const w=innerWidth,h=innerHeight; const portraitW=w<600; build after enemy loop maybe within always? Markers should hide when state.dead/victory or overlay. We can update each frame for each e:
if(!active){e.marker.style.display='none'; continue}
const dist... We already compute dist in loop but scoped. Could update markers in the same enemy loop after movement where dist available. But damage may remove enemy during attack earlier—no, attack occurs before frame? doAttack from input can remove. Enemies in state valid. Use:
const pv=e.group.position.clone();pv.y+=.9;pv.project(camera);
const sx=(pv.x*.5+.5)*w, sy=(-pv.y*.5+.5)*h;
const margin=20, top=portraitW?150:100, bottom=portraitW?h-170:h-120;
const vis=pv.z<1&&sx>-20&&sx<w+20&&sy>top&&sy<bottom; Wait if sy outside top because hidden under HUD, marker at top edge. But condition for "inside play area" should be full viewport for visibility; if enemy visible above top=150 but under HUD, do we need marker? It's visible on screen, so no. Use actual viewport bounds (0..w, 0..h). Then clamp marker within top/bottom safe. If inside screen but behind HUD, no marker (could be hidden by cards). Rare.
If !visible:
 marker.style.display='block';
 const cx=w/2, cy=h/2;
 const angle=Math.atan2(sy-cy,sx-cx);
 const tx=Math.max(22,Math.min(w-22,sx)); const ty=Math.max(portraitW?140:92,Math.min(portraitW?h-150:h-105,sy));
 marker.style.left=tx+'px'; marker.style.top=ty+'px'; marker.style.transform=`translate(-50%,-50%) rotate(${angle*180/Math.PI+90}deg)`;
But clamping sx to edges may place marker not exactly on edge if sy way out; still clamp both, so corners. Good.
Also hide if enemy dist>9? Use dist known in loop; add condition `dist<9.5`. But near offscreen at side x=±9, yes show. At spawn 10-11.8 hidden; they become visible markers after moving a bit. Fine. If whole wave offscreen, HUD count tells. Good.
if visible or dist>9.5 => none.

Marker color different for big? Could set border? add marker.style.color=e.big?'#ff936b':'#ffd078'. nice.

At spawn, marker appended. On death remove. On restart remove. On victory/death hide via active false loop.

Need include markers in cleanup: loop over enemies before removing. We already loop `for(const e of state.enemies)scene.remove(e.group);` add `e.marker?.remove()`.

Also on enemy death, remove marker before splice.

Let's patch.

